BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alcohol Ink Landscapes Workshop at Fiddleheads Gallery
DTSTART:20260915T180000
DTEND:20260915T193000
DTSTAMP:20260915T153719Z
UID:7f0b7155e2fc218eef7504f8901b9e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Discover the magic of alcohol inks as you create vibrant\, exp
 ressive landscapes inspired by nature. Through guided demonstrations and p
 layful experimentation\, you'll explore color\, movement\, and the beautif
 ul unpredictability of this exciting medium. No experience is necessary—
 just curiosity and a willingness to explore. You'll leave with a finished 
 artwork\, new techniques\, and the confidence to continue creating. All ma
 terials included.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fiddleheads Gallery\, Deerfield Valley Art Association\, 105 Main
  Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/alcohol-in
 k-landscapes-workshop-at-fiddleheads-gallery-10-08-2026-11-24-09
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fletcher Free's Fictional Book Club: Buckeye by Patrick Ryan
DTSTART:20260915T173000
DTEND:20260915T190000
DTSTAMP:20260915T153719Z
UID:b6675fc67528b324297592c7330e4a@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:In FFL's newest book club\, discuss how these fictional storie
 s and characters come to life (or don't) over snacks and coffee. Register 
 below or contact\, Barbara Shatara at bshatara@burlingtonvt.gov About This
  Month's Book: Buckeye by Patrick Ryan That\, as he saw it now\, was his l
 ife’s work: trying to make right what he’d gotten wrong. Wasn’t that
  a fair measure of a person\, what they did with their mistakes? In the ju
 bilant aftermath of the Allied victory in Europe\, Cal Jenkins\, a man wou
 nded not in war but by his inability to serve in it\, shares a single\, li
 fe-altering moment with Margaret Salt\, a woman determined to outrun her p
 ast. Cal is married to Becky\, whose spiritual gifts help the living speak
  to the dead\, while Margaret’s husband\, Felix\, is serving at sea\, be
 lieved to be safe—until a telegram suggests otherwise. What begins as a 
 fleeting transgression becomes a complex secret that irrevocably binds all
  four of them in unexpected ways. As their small Ohio town remakes itself 
 in the postwar boom\, the Salt and Jenkins families remain in each other
 ’s orbit\, and the consequences of choices made long ago begin to emerge
 \, reshaping their lives in ways that will forever impact the next generat
 ion. Sweeping yet intimate\, resplendent with moments of deep emotion and 
 unforgettable characters\, Buckeye is a transportive story of love\, loyal
 ty\, sacrifice\, and forgiveness. Limited copies of the book are available
  for checkout at the Main Desk.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fletcher Free Library\, 235 College St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/fletcher-f
 rees-fictional-book-club-buckeye-by-patrick-ryan-04-09-2026-22-44-51
END:VEVENT
